review October 22
Yes. Technical verdict: the trusted deterministic foundation is strong, but the student-facing architecture is only partially ready to achieve the mission. I would prioritize M3 and safety work before adding more LLM capability.

## Highest-priority findings

Domain ranges are not fully validated

The API accepts any finite mark, including negative values or marks above 100. It could calculate an invalid cutoff below 0 or above 200. Similar checks are missing for years, rounds, service years, and negative seat counts.

Relevant files:

tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/api/guidance-api.ts
tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/domain/validation.ts
tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/domain/admission-seat-fact.ts

Add domain-level bounded validators and tests. UI constraints alone are insufficient.

Two competing student experiences exist

The Tamil M2 journey follows the mission: progressive questions, unknown answers and guidance before marks.

The older reference page exposes the backend contract through a very large form containing rule-related fields, snapshots, quotas, rounds and raw enums. It is useful as engineering tooling but conflicts with the mission if treated as the real product.

Good path: tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/ui/m2-journey.ts
Technical form: tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/ui/student-guidance.ts

Make /journey the canonical product surface. Clearly isolate the reference form under development tooling.

Tamil presentation is fragmented

The general semantic presentation layer supports eligibility results only in English. Tamil result wording is separately hard-coded into the M2 renderer.

tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/student-semantics/catalogue.ts
tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/student-semantics/guidance-view.ts

M3 should introduce one bilingual presentation model containing:

verified result
understandable uncertainty
information still needed
things worth checking
next action
optional explanation
resolved source names and links

Both Tamil and English should render from this model rather than separate implementations.

Programme output can be misleading

When eligibility is NEEDS_REVIEW, the engine still returns all 18 mapped programmes. The UI calls them “Ordered programme choices,” even though eligibility is unresolved and no vacancy evidence exists.

tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/recommendation/foundation.ts
tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/src/ui/student-guidance.ts

Either suppress this list until sufficient evidence exists or label it as “programmes covered by this pilot,” not recommendations or choices.

Evidence ingestion is too brittle for yearly updates

Current concerns include:

Rules and source pages are hard-coded in TypeScript.
Reviewed Markdown is parsed at runtime using string splitting and regular expressions.
CSV parsing uses simple comma splitting and cannot safely handle quoted commas.
The year is globally frozen to 2026.

Create a versioned, schema-validated guidance bundle generated during review:

approved source documents
        ↓
reviewed structured JSON
        ↓
schema + provenance + freshness validation
        ↓
immutable yearly bundle
        ↓
deterministic engine and presentation

This will make 2027 updates safer and auditable.

Pilot hosting requires security work

The local server correctly avoids persistence and keeps marks out of URLs, but a hosted pilot should add:

request-size limits to every POST route
Cache-Control: no-store
security headers and CSP
HTTPS and controlled participant access
rate limiting
log redaction
explicit session expiry
privacy and consent handling

See tn-engineering-guidance-main/tn-engineering-guidance-main/scripts/mvp-server.mjs.

## What is already technically strong

Unknown and false values remain distinct.
Eligibility aggregation is conservative.
Cutoff and eligibility remain separate.
Every rule result carries provenance.
Unmapped programmes are excluded rather than guessed.
Missing vacancy is never interpreted as zero vacancy.
The LLM/RAG experiment is isolated from admission authority.
Tests cover deterministic behavior, provenance, unknown values and bilingual question routing.

## Recommended implementation order

Add domain range validation and adversarial tests.
Make the progressive journey the only student-facing personal-guidance path.
Implement the unified bilingual M3 result model.
Correct programme-list semantics for incomplete eligibility.
Replace runtime Markdown/naive CSV parsing with reviewed structured artifacts.
Add accessibility, mobile E2E and privacy/security checks.
Conduct real-student T04 validation.
Revisit LLM integration only after these foundations are accepted.

I attempted to run the test suite, but the runner produced no output and stalled in this workspace, so I interrupted it. The repository’s recorded baseline reports 211 passing tests, but I did not independently reconfirm that result during this review. 
